Sources for `qa` skill (see plans/skill-audits/qa.md for the full distribution matrix):

- gstack /qa (1642 LOC, "Test → Fix → Verify") — VENDORED (DEV-390): the QA methodology. Kept + distilled: the QA-engineer-AND-bug-fixer role, test-as-a-user (never read source to test), the modes (diff-aware default / full / quick / regression), the clean-working-tree precondition for atomic fix commits, the Orient → Explore → Document → Score → Triage → Fix-loop → Self-regulate → Report workflow, the per-page checklist (interactive / forms / navigation / empty-loading-error-overflow states / console-after-every-interaction / responsive), the two evidence tiers (interactive before/after vs static single shot), the health-score rubric (per-category deductions + weights), the atomic `fix(qa):` commit-per-fix + re-verify + regression-test + verified/best-effort/reverted classification, and the WTF self-regulation stop-and-ask heuristic.
- gstack /qa-only (1214 LOC) — VENDORED as the `--report-only` mode (phases through Report, no fix loop). No second skill: report-only is a mode, not a subject.
- gstack /design-review (1952 LOC), live half — the live-screenshot visual QA is re-homed here as the "visual pass" that COMPOSES `ui-review` (which already owns the visual-craft methodology: register split, squint test, interaction-state coverage, technical audit). This skill drives the browser; ui-review supplies the bar. No duplication.
- REPOINTED, not ported: every gstack `$B <cmd>` browse-daemon call (goto/snapshot/click/fill/console/viewport/screenshot) maps onto the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` MCP tools (navigate/computer/read_page/form_input/read_console_messages/resize_window/gif_creator/read_network_requests), with `tabs_context_mcp` called first. Full daemon port was ~190 CDP/Chromium files and weeks of work; the re-point is the same prose on a browser layer Claude Code already ships. This IS the epic's "Vague 4" claude-in-chrome re-point.
- REJECTED (gstack runtime, not doctrine): the browse binary + `./setup` + bun bootstrap, CDP-mode detection, gbrain/learnings search + log, telemetry/review-log, the `~/.gstack/projects` + chromium-profile cookie import (claude-in-chrome uses the user's real logged-in Chrome, so cookie import is moot — documented as a rejection per the ticket), TESTING.md / CLAUDE.md auto-edit.
- REJECTED (scope creep, routed elsewhere): the entire Test-Framework-Bootstrap block (detect runtime → research → install → write TESTING.md). Standing up a test framework is `tdd`/`testing`, not QA. A QA skill that also bootstraps a framework is two subjects; the ticket's "un sujet, un skill" forbids it.

Strategy: distill + repoint. One skill, one subject ("live browser QA of a running web app"). qa-only folds in as a mode; the visual pass composes ui-review; the regression test composes tdd/testing. < 30% overlap is structural: this drives the browser + functional/fix loop; ui-review judges visuals; devex-audit audits dev surfaces; tdd/testing author suites.

Companion change (same ticket, gated by Folpe): the "Never use mcp__claude-in-chrome__*" rule in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md predates the claude-in-chrome adoption and makes this skill unusable; it is lifted in the same move.

DEV-444 adaptation: UI evidence now covers mobile and desktop applicable states, carries the current
diff identity, and is handed to a fresh Visual Craft Director; unavailable browser proof blocks.
